# Auto-DJ: GLO held, F5 (key 24) on, its groove length on the PERFORM edit page (8, 16, 32, 64 bars), G5 (key 26)
# a new piece each round. A groove, a drum fill in its last bar, a breakdown, a build (the riser held), the drop,
# and the groove again, on the bar clock. The timings below are for the first piece (seed 0).
seed 0
wait 1500
# the groove length (8 bars) is on the PERFORM edit page now (the key it was on is the pluck's solo): SEL + FX, to page 17, Groove
press SEL
tap FX
release SEL
wait 100
spin SELECT 1
wait 30
spin SELECT 1
wait 30
spin SELECT 1
wait 30
spin SELECT 1
wait 30
spin SELECT 1
wait 30
spin SELECT 1
wait 30
spin SELECT 1
wait 30
spin SELECT 1
wait 30
spin SELECT 1
wait 30
spin SELECT 1
wait 30
spin SELECT 1
wait 30
spin SELECT 1
wait 30
spin SELECT 1
wait 30
spin SELECT 1
wait 30
spin SELECT 1
wait 30
spin SELECT 1
wait 30
spin K2 -1
wait 50
expect djlen 0
tap FX
wait 100
press GLO
tapkey 24
release GLO
expect djon 1
expect piece 0
wait 11700
# 12 s: the groove, bars counting
expect djphase 0
expect sec 0
wait 6000
# 18 s: the breakdown
expect djphase 1
expect sec 1
wait 7500
# 25 s: the build, the riser held by the DJ
expect djphase 2
expect sec 2
expect fxmask 16777216
wait 11000
# 36 s: the groove again, the riser let go
expect djphase 0
expect sec 0
expect fxmask 0
# off: it stops running the sections
press GLO
tapkey 24
release GLO
expect djon 0
wait 22000
expect sec 0
# new pieces on: one round later the next piece plays
press GLO
tapkey 24
tapkey 26
release GLO
expect djon 1
wait 24000
expect piece 1
